title: handoff: what the last agent left behind
effort: S
area: format

A place for an agent to record where it got to when it drops a claim without
finishing, so the next agent does not reconstruct it from the diff.

A project field, not a header line. It fails the test the header has to pass
— it does not help answer "can I start this?" — and a structural line is a
cost every ticket carries forever, the same reason priority stayed a field.
Ships in the default schema; costs nothing for projects that drop it.

One line, deliberately. A multi-line dump invites an agent to paste its
reasoning, which is the context bloat the format fights. Overwritten rather
than accumulated, so it describes the most recent stop instead of growing
into an unread log.

Written by `pidly release -m`, shown by `status`, and printed by `claim` —
that last one is the point, since a note nobody is shown is a note nobody
reads.

Also covers the resolution note that closing lost when the marker file went
away.

Writing the tests surfaced that release only succeeds for the process that
claimed, so an agent must export PIDLY_PID once for its lifetime rather than
per invocation. That was already the design; it is now written down in the
shipped reference, where it was missing.

Done: implemented in bin/pidly, covered by tests/handoff.sh (14 cases).
